"""Apply reviewed v6 clarifications to the embedded baseline; never edit frozen inputs."""
def once(text,old,new):
    assert text.count(old)==1,('Expected one inherited contract marker',old[:95],text.count(old))
    return text.replace(old,new,1)

def correct(text):
    text=once(text,'Partial commit freezes committed attributes; later suffix cancellation cannot erase that prefix.','Partial commit freezes accepted content/attributes against residual cancellation; a later explicitly admitted and accepted replacement may supersede that content. Cancellation alone never deletes its current accepted incarnation.')
    text=once(text,'The new marked interval is `[0, (oldM1-oldM0)-k)`, NOT based on the whole overlay length.','For k=0, the overlay, committed cover, attribution baseline and marked interval `[oldM0,oldM1)` are unchanged; only an explicit valid selection/session event and settlement-evidence invalidation apply. No preceding island or cell-clearing prelude is accepted. For k>0 only, the new marked interval is `[0, (oldM1-oldM0)-k)`, NOT based on the whole overlay length.')
    text=once(text,'Partial commit invalidates outstanding settlement evidence and creates a new attribution baseline for the remaining active interval; it creates no standalone history entry.','Partial commit invalidates outstanding settlement evidence; only a positive count creates a new attribution baseline for the residual interval. It creates no standalone history entry.')
    text=once(text,'Composition formatting targets the semantic constituent islands plus accepted session portions, never the convex hull and never untouched bridged text.','On terminal acceptance, composition formatting targets the semantic constituent islands plus accepted session portions, never the convex hull and never untouched bridged text. Explicit application abort cancels pending CompositionTarget formatting with CompositionCancelled even when partially accepted text survives; unrelated explicit-range commands retain their ordinary mapping rules.')
    text=once(text,'Accepted surviving session text remains the target.','Accepted surviving session text remains the target on terminal acceptance, but does not override explicit abort/lifecycle cancellation.')
    text=once(text,'A composition-target format whose final semantic target is empty returns Cancelled(TargetDeleted) with one CommandWithoutHistory credit.','On ordinary terminal acceptance, a composition-target format whose final semantic target is empty returns Cancelled(TargetDeleted) with one CommandWithoutHistory credit. Explicit abort instead cancels that pending format with CompositionCancelled, including when accepted partial text survives, and contributes the same one-use attempted-action credit.')
    text=once(text,'Nested and merged tables remain outside the fixed product scope.','Merged/split cells are required F15 work under S0 and the v6 D03 span/identity contract. Nested tables remain an explicit owner scope decision. This earlier unspanned insertTable model does not implement merged cells.')
    text=once(text,'An explicitly deleted flow always marks affected anchors deleted and supplies a legal fallback point.','Before retiring a flow, relocate anchors whose target NodeId/text survives a move into another flow. Anchors still targeting removed content or the retired container are deleted/orphaned and receive a legal UI fallback; that fallback is not a new semantic attachment. Apply v6 D03 for merged cells and review anchors.')
    text=once(text,'A cell selection retains directional endpoint CellIds but enumerates its rectangle in row-major order.','A cell selection retains directional endpoint CellIds. For spans, first compute fixed-point span closure and enumerate distinct CellIds by origin row-major order as specified in v6 D03; repeated grid slots do not declare duplicate canonical flows.')
    # Keep the prior abort example because v6 explicitly selects that policy.
    text=once(text,'Every admitted history-producing command contributes either its actual new history ID or one ephemeral `CommandWithoutHistory` slot if cancelled/rejected/no-op.','Every admitted history-producing command contributes either its actual new history ID or one ephemeral `CommandWithoutHistory` slot if cancelled/rejected/no-op, including when a preceding queued Undo removed its target. This is an intentional attempted-action policy; unused credits are discarded after this drainage and never survive into a later ordinary Undo.')
    return text
